title: Tree View
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

A tree view diagram renders a file and folder hierarchy with automatic icon detection based on file extensions. Use it for project structure documentation, repository layouts, and directory tree references. ''New in Mermaid 11.'' Uses `treeView-beta`.

---

!! Basic example

```
treeView-beta
    "project"/
        "src"/
            "app.ts"
            "utils.ts"
        "package.json"
        "README.md"
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
treeView-beta
    "project"/
        "src"/
            "app.ts"
            "utils.ts"
        "package.json"
        "README.md"
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: TypeScript web application repository layout

This example shows a typical full-stack TypeScript project structure with source, tests, configuration, and documentation files. Known extensions auto-map to icons; trailing `/` marks directories.

```
%%{init: {"treeView": {"rowIndent": 20}}}%%
treeView-beta
    accTitle: TypeScript web app project structure
    accDescr: File and folder hierarchy for a full-stack TypeScript web application

    %% ── Root ────────────────────────────────────────
    "webapp"/
        %% ── Application source ──────────────────────
        "src"/
            "server"/
                "app.ts"
                "router.ts"
                "middleware.ts"
            "client"/
                "index.html"
                "main.ts"
                "styles.css"
            "shared"/
                "types.ts"
                "utils.ts"

        %% ── Tests ───────────────────────────────────
        "tests"/
            "server.test.ts"
            "client.test.ts"
            "utils.test.ts"

        %% ── Configuration and docs ──────────────────
        "package.json"
        "tsconfig.json"
        ".gitignore"
        "README.md"
        "Dockerfile"
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
