---

!! Syntax

```
treeView-beta
    "Root Folder"/
        "Subfolder"/
            "file.ts"
            "file.json"
        "root-file.md"
```

''Trailing `/`'' marks a directory node (displayed with a folder icon and bold label). Files without `/` use icons determined by their extension.

|!Pattern|!Result|
|`"name"/`|Directory node|
|`"name.ts"`|TypeScript file icon|
|`"name.json"`|JSON file icon|
|`"name.md"`|Markdown file icon|
|`"name.html"`|HTML file icon|
|`"name.css"`|CSS file icon|
|`"name.py"`|Python file icon|
|`"Dockerfile"`|Docker icon|
|`".gitignore"`|Git ignore icon|

''Config:'' `%%{init: {"treeView": {"rowIndent": 20}}}%%` widens the indentation between levels.

!! Tips

* Use `treeView-beta` with exact camelCase — `treeview-beta` (lowercase v) will not parse.
* Indentation defines hierarchy — use spaces, not tabs, to avoid silent hierarchy collapse.
* No edges or connections; `treeView-beta` is a purely hierarchical display.
* `treeView-beta` is still beta — syntax may evolve in future Mermaid versions.

